    "body": "> I guess we should only report for the document that ends up replacing the initial about:blank document and only if that document was fetched over HTTP.\r\n\r\nFor the [old processing model](https://github.com/w3c/resource-timing/pull/177/files#diff-0eb547304658805aad788d320f10bf1f292797b5e6d745a3bf617584da017051R942), we landed on aborting the reporting when the request wasn't triggered by \"process the {i,}frame attributes\". We can probably do something similar on the reporting side in HTML. ",
